===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[overly|Overly]] [[patriotic]] or [[nationalistic]], often with an element of favouring [[war#Noun|war]] or an [[aggressive]] [[foreign policy]].
#: {{ux|en|My editorial angered both the '''jingoistic''' war hawks and the anti-war protesters.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Joseph McCabe|authorlink=Joseph McCabe|chapter=The Responsibility of the Churches|title=The War and the Churches|location=London|publisher=Watts & Co. 17 Johnson's Court, {{w|Fleet Street}}, E.C.|year=1915|page=22|pageurl=https://ia601401.us.archive.org/13/items/warandchurches00mccauoft/warandchurches00mccauoft.pdf#page=40|oclc=44160030|passage=The truth is that all classes—Christian and non-Christian—have yielded fatally to the pernicious interpretation which interested politicians, soldiers, manufacturers, and '''Jingoistic''' writers have put on the real economic needs of the country.}}
#* {{RQ:Mencken American Language|section=§ 2|chapter=14|page=86|passage=All this '''jingoistic''' bombast, however, was directed toward defending, not so much the national vernacular as the national ''belles lettres''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|editors=[[w:Robert Freitas|Robert A. Freitas, Jr.]], and William P. Gilbreath|chapter=Replicating Systems Concepts: Self-replicating Lunar Factory and Demonstration|title=Advanced Automation for Space Missions {{...|Proceedings of the 1980 NASA/ASEE Summer Study Sponsored by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration and the American Society for Engineering Education Held at the University of Santa Clara, Santa Clara, California, June 23&nbsp;– August 29, 1980}}|series=NASA Conference Publication|seriesvolume=2255|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher={{w|National Aeronautics and Space Administration}} Scientific and Technical Information Branch|year=1982|page=244|pageurl=https://archive.org/stream/NASA_NTRS_Archive_19830007077#page/n249/mode/1up/|column=2|oclc=704458371|passage=If we continue to be limited to our exceedingly fragile existence on spaceship Earth, a natural disaster or our own '''jingoistic''' or ecological foolhardiness is almost certain to terminate our existence perhaps centuries or millenia{{sic|millennia}} from today.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Harvey Araton|title=Jingoism Is the Way of the Olympics|work=The New York Times|date=2002-02-07|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2002/02/07/sports/sports-of-the-times-jingoism-is-the-way-of-the-olympics.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=But are these Olympics also destined to become a '''jingoistic''', flag-waving convention, a world-alienating Patriot Games?}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=The Observer view on triggering article 50: As Britain hurtles towards the precipice, truth and democracy are in short supply|url=https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2017/mar/26/observer-editorial-triggering-of-article-50-jeopardises-60-years-of-unparalleled-peace|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20170517091650/https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2017/mar/26/observer-editorial-triggering-of-article-50-jeopardises-60-years-of-unparalleled-peace|archivedate=17 May 2017|newspaper={{w|The Observer}}|location=London|date=27 March 2017|passage=This approach plays fast and loose with ordinary people's livelihoods. Yet still, with '''jingoistic''' horns and trumpets drowning out the roar of the deep, the stampede towards the cliff's edge gathers pace.}}

